  "edge_lattices/edge_lattices_provenance.md": "edge_lattices/edge_lattices_provenance.txt",
  "note": "Partial human reconstruction of RH and Dirichlet GRH. The actual host Hecke-character frame and determinant data, local arithmetic level/character comparisons and conditional weight/series reading are expanded. Same-base initial coefficient, jet and bare later-stage constructions are joined with their exact compatibility boundaries. Primitive finite theta-test arithmetic, fixed-field sum and finite-support deductions are reconstructed with remaining analytic, separation, period and operator inputs explicit. The literal quantitative mass window is proved from SiegelMassRatioCM, including actual Euler products, local indices and Vandermonde estimates; exact prime-count and scale transports retain their uniform analytic/arithmetic suppliers. Classical nonvanishing at one gives the bounded-modulus real-zero margin. Compatible nonempty arithmetic/geometric realization, global mass and weighted prime-window inputs, the remaining primitive theta identities and the four global branches remain. No complete self-contained RH/GRH proof, full Lean build or independent kernel replay is asserted. Twenty v0.18 root files are preserved under history/version_0_18/. The last rendered PDF remains in history/version_0_13/. Current v0.19 locations use section labels and claim IDs; no current page numbers are asserted.",
